How can I find the mean, median, and standard deviation of "score" in "df" but only for values greater than or equal to 5 using only one line of Java code? Here's the code I have so far:
df.stream().filter(x -> x.getScore() >= 5).collect(Collectors.teeing(
 Collectors.averagingDouble(x -> x.getScore()),
 Collectors.collectingAndThen(Collectors.toList(), list -> {
 Collections.sort(list, Comparator.comparingDouble(x -> x.getScore()));
 double median;
 int size = list.size();
 if (size % 2 == 0) {
 median = (list.get(size/2 - 1).getScore() + list.get(size/2).getScore()) / 2.0;
 } else {
 median = list.get(size/2).getScore();
 }
 return median;
 }),
 Collectors.collectingAndThen(Collectors.toList(), list -> {
 double sum = 0.0, sumSquare = 0.0;
 int n = list.size();
 for (Data d : list) {
 sum += d.getScore();
 sumSquare += d.getScore() * d.getScore();
 }
 double stdev = Math.sqrt((n * sumSquare - sum * sum) / (n * (n - 1)));
 return stdev;
 })
));

