How can you modify the sample code to include more customer-specific information such as the product name, date of purchase, and specific issue? 
Here is the table with the necessary customer data:
| First Name | Last Name | Email | Product Name | Date of Purchase | Specific Issue |
|------------|-----------|--------------------|--------------|-----------------|----------------------|
| John | Smith | j.smith@example.com | Product A | 2022-03-15 | Issue with functionality |
| Sarah | Lee | s.lee@example.com | Product B | 2022-02-28 | Shipping delay |
| Michael | Brown | m.brown@example.com | Product C | 2022-01-19 | Defective parts |
And here is the modified code with personalized sentences:
complaints = [
 "The issue you experienced with " + customer_data(4) + " is a top priority for us. We apologize for any inconvenience caused.";
 "Thank you for bringing to our attention the issue you faced with " + customer_data(4) + ". We are working to resolve it as soon as possible.";
 "We are sorry to hear that you have encountered an issue with " + customer_data(4) + ". We will do everything we can to make it right for you."
];
customer_data = [
 "John", "Smith", "j.smith@example.com", "Product A", "2022-03-15", "Issue with functionality"
];
for i = 1:numel(complaints)
 % Customize sentence based on customer data
 sentence1 = "Dear " + customer_data(1) + " " + customer_data(2) + ", " + complaints(i);
 sentence2 = "We have forwarded your complaint regarding " + customer_data(4) + " (purchased on " + customer_data(5) + ") and the issue with " + customer_data(6) + " to our support team. They will contact you at " + customer_data(3) + " to resolve the issue.";

 % Send email with personalized sentences
 send_email(customer_data(3), sentence1, sentence2);
end
Note: The send_email() function is not included in this code as it may vary depending on the email service being used.

